<HelpChapterSection Id="signing">
    <HelpTopicSection Id="signing-how">
        <p>KOD applies a <strong>qualified electronic signature (QES)</strong> using IIT's official “CSK User” library — the same one used by the Diia portal (ID.GOV.UA). The signature has the same legal force as a handwritten one.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>The key and password never leave your device.</strong> The key file is read in the browser, in a separate protected thread (Web Worker). Neither the key nor its password is sent to the server.</li>
            <li>Only public service requests to the provider go through the server: certificate status checks (OCSP) and obtaining a timestamp (TSP — only the data hash is sent, not the document itself).</li>
            <li>The key is released from memory right after signing, and also when you go back in the wizard, close the signing window or leave the page.</li>
            <li>The server updates the list of providers and their certificates from IIT's official source twice a day, so keys with new or reissued certificates work without any extra setup.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Where the signature is used:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Signing documents</strong> in the “Documents” module — the signature is stored in the system together with the document (see “<a href="/help#documents-sign">Signing a document</a>”).</li>
            <li><strong>Signing any files</strong> on the <span class="help-ui">Signing</span> page — you download the result to your device; nothing is stored in the system.</li>
            <li><strong>Verifying signed files</strong> on the <span class="help-ui">Verify</span> tab.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="signing-keys">
        <p><strong>File keys</strong> from all qualified trust service providers (QTSPs) on the Central Certification Authority's list are supported: the State Tax Service, Diia, PrivatBank, monobank, Oschadbank, PUMB, Ukrgasbank, DepositSign, Vchasno, MASTERKEY, the Treasury and others — more than 30 providers.</p>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>File type</th><th>Where it comes from</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Key-6.dat</td><td>The classic key of most providers (State Tax Service, Diia and others). Certificates are found automatically.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>*.pfx, *.p12</td><td>A PKCS#12 container (often PrivatBank and bank QTSPs).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>*.jks</td><td>Java KeyStore (PrivatBank and others).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>*.pk8, *.zs2</td><td>Other key container formats.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p>Usually leave the <span class="help-ui">Trust service provider</span> field set to <span class="help-ui">Detect automatically</span>. Select a specific provider only if automatic detection didn't work.</p>
        <p>If the provider doesn't support automatic certificate download, expand <span class="help-ui">Add certificates manually (if the provider doesn't support automatic download)</span> and add the <code class="ds-code">*.cer</code>, <code class="ds-code">*.crt</code> or <code class="ds-code">*.p7b</code> certificate files issued to you by the provider.</p>
        <Alert Tone="Tone.Outline" Icon="info" Title="Hardware tokens and cloud keys">The “Hardware token” options (Almaz-1K, Krystal-1 tokens, etc.) and “Cloud / Diia.Signature” are shown as disabled: they require separate provider components (the IIT web agent or a cloud signing service) that are not connected to KOD at the moment.</Alert>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="signing-wizard">
        <p>Open <span class="help-ui">Signing</span> in the menu. The <span class="help-ui">Sign</span> tab contains a three-step wizard. The top of the page shows which step you're on; you can return to a completed step with the <span class="help-ui">Back</span> button or by clicking its number.</p>
        <h4>Step 1. Files</h4>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Drag files into the <span class="help-ui">Drag files here or click to select</span> area, or click it and select the files.</li>
            <li>A list of files with their sizes appears below the area. Each file can be up to <strong>25 MB</strong>.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Next</span>. The button is enabled only when at least one file is selected.</li>
        </ol>
        <h4>Step 2. Parameters</h4>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Choose the <span class="help-ui">Signature format</span>. Formats unavailable for the selected files are disabled (for example, PAdES is only for PDF; CAdES and ASiC-S are only for a single file).</li>
            <li>For CAdES and XAdES, choose the <span class="help-ui">Signature type</span>: <span class="help-ui">Detached</span> (the signature file sits next to the document) or <span class="help-ui">Enveloped</span> (the data is inside the signature).</li>
            <li>Choose the <span class="help-ui">Signature level</span>. <strong>B-LT</strong> is recommended — it contains everything needed for verification years later.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Next</span>. How to choose a format — see “<a href="/help#signing-formats">Signature formats and levels</a>”.</li>
        </ol>
        <h4>Step 3. Key and signature</h4>
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Check the summary at the top: which files, format and level will be used.</li>
            <li>Key type — <span class="help-ui">File key</span>. Leave the provider set to <span class="help-ui">Detect automatically</span>.</li>
            <li>Select the key file in the <span class="help-ui">Select the key file</span> area.</li>
            <li>Enter the <span class="help-ui">Key password</span> and click <span class="help-ui">Read key</span> (or press Enter). The password is cleared from the field immediately.</li>
            <li>The key owner card appears: full name, organization, position, individual tax number / EDRPOU code, provider, certificate number and validity period. Make sure this is your key. You can choose a different key with the <span class="help-ui">Another key</span> button.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Sign</span>.</li>
            <li>After successful signing, “File signed” appears with the format, level and time. Click <span class="help-ui">Download …</span> to save the result. To sign other files, click <span class="help-ui">Sign other files</span> — you'll need to read the key again.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The link to the signed file is valid for 10 minutes — save the file right away.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="signing-formats">
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Result</th><th>When to choose</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>CAdES</td><td><code class="ds-code">*.p7s</code></td><td>A universal format for any single file. “Detached” — the signature file sits next to the original; “Enveloped” — a single file containing both the document and the signature. The most common format in Ukraine.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>XAdES</td><td><code class="ds-code">*.xml</code></td><td>An XML signature; several files can be signed at once. Needed if the recipient requires XML.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>PAdES</td><td><code class="ds-code">*_signed.pdf</code></td><td>A signature inside the PDF — the document opens in a regular PDF viewer. Only for a single PDF file.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>ASiC-S</td><td><code class="ds-code">*.asics</code></td><td>A container (ZIP) with one file and its signature. A European standard.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>ASiC-E</td><td><code class="ds-code">*.asice</code></td><td>A container with several files and one signature covering all of them.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>What it contains</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>B-B — basic</td><td>Only the signature and the certificate. The signing time comes from your computer's clock.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>B-T — with a timestamp</td><td>Adds a qualified timestamp from the provider: a precise, provable signing time.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>B-LT — with long-term validation data</td><td>Plus the certificate status at the moment of signing (OCSP) and the certificate chain. The signature can be verified years later, even after the certificate has expired. <strong>Recommended.</strong></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>B-LTA — archival</td><td>Plus an archival timestamp for long-term storage over many years.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="signing-verify">
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Open <span class="help-ui">Signing</span> → the <span class="help-ui">Verify</span> tab.</li>
            <li>Drag in the signed file (<code class="ds-code">*.p7s</code>, <code class="ds-code">*.pdf</code>, <code class="ds-code">*.xml</code>, <code class="ds-code">*.asics</code>, <code class="ds-code">*.asice</code>). For a detached signature, also add the original file.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Verify</span>.</li>
            <li>If the signatures are valid, “Signatures are valid” appears with the format, container name and number of signatures, and for each signature — the signer's full name, organization, individual tax number / EDRPOU code, provider, certificate number and signing time (or timestamp).</li>
            <li>If the signature contains the data inside, the <span class="help-ui">Download …</span> button lets you save the original document.</li>
            <li>If verification fails, “Verification failed” appears with an explanation of the reason.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Verification takes place in your browser — the file is not sent to the server.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="signing-problems">
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Wrong password or damaged key file.</td><td>Check the keyboard layout and Caps Lock, and select the right file (the key file itself, for example Key-6.dat, not a certificate).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>The key certificate could not be found. Select the provider manually or add certificate files.</td><td>Select your provider in the list instead of “Detect automatically”, or add certificates via “Add certificates manually”.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>The key certificate has expired or is not yet valid.</td><td>The key has expired — get a new one from your provider.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>The key certificate has been revoked (it is on the revocation list).</td><td>The key has been blocked by the provider. Contact the provider to get a new one.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Could not obtain a timestamp. Try the B-B signature level or try again later.</td><td>The provider's timestamp server is temporarily unavailable. Try again in a few minutes; if the signature is urgent, choose the B-B level.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Could not check the certificate status (OCSP). Try again later.</td><td>The provider's server is temporarily unavailable. Try again later.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>No connection to the provider's server (CA). Check your connection and try again.</td><td>Check your internet connection and try again.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Files larger than 25 MB are not supported.</td><td>Reduce the file size (for example, compress the PDF) or split it into parts.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Could not load the signing library.</td><td>Refresh the page. The library is several megabytes in size and loads when the signing panel opens.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>This is a detached signature: also add the file that was signed.</td><td>When verifying, add the original document together with the signature file.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>No signatures found in the file.</td><td>The selected file doesn't contain a signature — make sure you uploaded the signed file.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </HelpTopicSection>
</HelpChapterSection>
